>> title: Butter Beans
>> category: Rice, Beans & Grains
>> tags: beans, pork, southern, stew, side
>> counters: Meat and Three, One Pot
>> aka: lima beans, baby limas, large limas, butterbeans, speckled butter beans
>> servings: 8
>> time: 1 hr 40 min
>> slack: unforgiving — butter beans that stay whole and separate are undercooked, and a few of them have to break up and thicken the pot before it is done; that is a doneness test rather than a timer, and no amount of butter at the end makes an underdone bean edible
>> pairs-with: ham-hock-stock, skillet-cornbread, oxtails, collard-greens
>> step.1: Cook these until a few of them break up and thicken the pot. Butter beans that stay whole and separate are undercooked, and the liquid is meant to go creamy with no cream anywhere in it.
>> step.2: render 8 min
>> step.3: sweat 6 min
>> step.4: simmer covered 1 hr 10 min
>> step.5: butter and salt at the end

Cook these until a few of them break up and thicken the pot. Butter beans that stay whole and separate are undercooked, and the liquid is meant to go creamy with no cream anywhere in it.

Render @salt pork{3%oz}(85 g; diced) in a #Dutch oven{} for ~render{8%min}.

Sweat @&(~1)salt pork{} with @yellow onion{1%medium}(diced) for ~sweat{6%min}.

Simmer @&(~1)pork base{} covered with @dried lima beans{1%lb}(450 g; soaked overnight), @ham hock stock{2%qt}(1.9 L), @bay leaf{1}, @black pepper{1%tsp} for ~simmer{70%min}.

Stir @&(~1)beans{} with @unsalted butter{3%Tbs}(42 g), @kosher salt{2%tsp}.

Mash a ladleful against the side of the pot and stir it back in if the liquid is still thin. That is the only thickening this side ever gets.
